🧠 AI Features (RAG-Powered)

DailyDeck includes an AI assistant built using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to provide context-aware help across tasks and notes.

How It Works
User Query → Embeddings → Vector Search → Context → Claude AI → Response

Tech Stack
LLM: Claude Sonnet 4
Embeddings: Anthropic text embeddings
Vector DB: MongoDB Atlas Vector Search
Backend: Node.js API

Key Capabilities
🔍 Natural Language Search
Semantic search across tasks and notes
Understands dev terms (PRs, deployments, deadlines)
Supports time-based queries (last week, overdue, upcoming)

🧾 Smart Summaries
Summarizes progress across related tasks and notes
Highlights blockers and next steps

📚 Context-Aware Answers
Finds past decisions from notes
Returns citation-based responses with source links
🛠 Intelligent Task Creation
Converts feature requests into structured subtasks
Suggests priorities, tags, and dependencies

API Example
POST /api/ai/query
{
  "query": "What are my blockers this week?",
  "context": ["tasks", "notes"],
  "mode": "search | summarize | generate"
}

RAG Flow (Simplified)

Generate embedding for user query
Perform vector search (MongoDB Atlas)
Assemble most relevant context
Send context + query to Claude
Performance & Security
Server-side embeddings (no client exposure)
User-isolated data access
Cached frequent queries (5-min TTL)
Optimized context to stay within token limits

